{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-54b5f2e1-251d-404d-86ac-06556f3fcb31","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8252d008195df699","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9001-9zm_dp03/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9001-E001.md","content":"# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe InferenceService models directly in the RHOAI Dashboard model serving views, so data scientists can tell whether a deployment is healthy without leaving the console or using `oc` / Kubernetes events. It adds a per-model status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) to the deployed models views, a status detail view exposing the underlying condition messages and recent events for failed or progressing deployments, near-real-time refresh of the displayed status, and filter/sort by status on the deployed models list.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Derive a deployment status of Ready, Progressing, or Failed for each deployed KServe InferenceService from the InferenceService CR status conditions (e.g., Ready, PredictorReady) and recent Kubernetes events, as exposed by KServe today — no KServe-side changes.\n- Display the derived status for each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n- Add a status detail view that shows the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n- Ensure the displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n- Add filter and sort controls for the deployed models list by status.\n- Validate that the Dashboard's status mapping matches the actual InferenceService status conditions and Kubernetes events (KServe is passive in this strategy — this validation is part of this epic's deliverable, not a KServe change).\n- Out of scope: alerting or notifications on status transitions; status history / timeline views; ModelMesh deployments (KServe InferenceService only).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed model whose InferenceService is Ready, when the user opens the model serving view, then the model is shown with status Ready.\n- Given a model whose deployment is failed or progressing, when the user opens the status detail view, then the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent Kubernetes events are shown.\n- Given a change in the actual InferenceService state, when 30 seconds have elapsed, then the displayed status reflects the new state without a manual page reload.\n- Given the deployed models list, when the user filters or sorts by status, then the list is filtered or ordered accordingly.\n- The status mapping (Ready / Progressing / Failed derivation) is validated against actual InferenceService CR status conditions and Kubernetes events as documented for KServe, with no changes required to KServe.\n- No status-related alerts/notifications, status history, or timeline views are introduced by this change.\n- ModelMesh deployments are not covered by the status surface (KServe InferenceService only).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Users see a deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n- HLR-2 (P0): Users can open a status detail view showing the underlying condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n- HLR-3 (P1): Displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n- HLR-4 (P2): Users can filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24820,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de35a776a263547","agent_id":"ad75af054d482c709","ses