{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bef3e2885a8db15f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E001\n3\ttitle: Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe InferenceService models directly in the RHOAI Dashboard model serving views, so data scientists can tell whether a deployment is healthy without leaving the console or using `oc` / Kubernetes events. It adds a per-model status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) to the deployed models views, a status detail view exposing the underlying condition messages and recent events for failed or progressing deployments, near-real-time refresh of the displayed status, and filter/sort by status on the deployed models list.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Derive a deployment status of Ready, Progressing, or Failed for each deployed KServe InferenceService from the InferenceService CR status conditions (e.g., Ready, PredictorReady) and recent Kubernetes events, as exposed by KServe today — no KServe-side changes.\n38\t- Display the derived status for each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n39\t- Add a status detail view that shows the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n40\t- Ensure the displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n41\t- Add filter and sort controls for the deployed models list by status.\n42\t- Validate that the Dashboard's status mapping matches the actual InferenceService status conditions and Kubernetes events (KServe is passive in this strategy — this validation is part of this epic's deliverable, not a KServe change).\n43\t- Out of scope: alerting or notifications on status transitions; status history / timeline views; ModelMesh deployments (KServe InferenceService only).\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a deployed model whose InferenceService is Ready, when the user opens the model serving view, then the model is shown with status Ready.\n48\t- Given a model whose deployment is failed or progressing, when the user opens the status detail view, then the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent Kubernetes events are shown.\n49\t- Given a change in the actual InferenceService state, when 30 seconds have elapsed, then the displayed status reflects the new state without a manual page reload.\n50\t- Given the deployed models list, when the user filters or sorts by status, then the list is filtered or ordered accordingly.\n51\t- The status mapping (Ready / Progressing / Failed derivation) is validated against actual InferenceService CR status conditions and Kubernetes events as documented for KServe, with no changes required to KServe.\n52\t- No status-related alerts/notifications, status history, or timeline views are introduced by this change.\n53\t- ModelMesh deployments are not covered by the status surface (KServe InferenceService only).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-1 (P0): Users see a deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n58\t- HLR-2 (P0): Users can open a status detail view showing the underlying condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n59\t- HLR-3 (P1): Displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n60\t- HLR-4 (P2): Users can filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-870f01c376fda592","agent_id":"ab4d9bd43bd0e0d00","session_id":"43f64084-1d69-4055-a8f7-bc56aec5e245","uuid":"6fc2f89e-84f7-4eaa-b5dd-d1898a12915a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:18:17.982Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bef3e2885a8db15f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9001 decomposition"}
