{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e340e9c4-0e6b-403a-a2ee-711d844c6a97","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c5bd53b6dfc2536","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9001-9zm_dp03/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9001-E004.md","content":"# Filter and sort the deployed models list by status\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic adds filter and sort controls for the deployed models list in the RHOAI Dashboard model serving views, so users can narrow the list to a given deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) and order it by status. It builds on the per-model status column delivered by the P0 status-surface work for model serving.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add filter controls to the deployed models list, allowing users to filter the list by deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed).\n- Add sort controls, allowing users to order the deployed models list by status.\n- No KServe-side changes: the status values filtered and sorted on are the ones derived Dashboard-side from the InferenceService status conditions and Kubernetes events.\n- Out of scope: alerting or notifications on status transitions; status history / timeline views; ModelMesh deployments (KServe InferenceService only).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the deployed models list showing models with mixed statuses, when the user filters by status Failed, then only models with status Failed are shown.\n- Given the deployed models list, when the user sorts by status, then the list is ordered by status accordingly.\n- Given no filter or sort selected, when the user opens the deployed models list, then the default unfiltered and unsorted list is shown.\n- No status-related alerts/notifications, status history, or timeline views are introduced by this change.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): Users can filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/gl