{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1dcb99e6ab1d32","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-9001 — Surface model deployment status in the RHOAI Dashboard\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 | Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 | Near-real-time refresh of deployment status in Dashboard model serving views | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 | Filter and sort the deployed models list by status | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P2 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E002 | Document deployment status values and Failed-deployment troubleshooting | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n20\t\n21\t## Dependency DAG\n22\t\n23\t```mermaid\n24\tgraph TD\n25\t    RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9001-E002\n26\t    RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9001-E003\n27\t    RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9001-E004\n28\t    RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 --> RHAISTRAT-9001-E002\n29\t    RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 --> RHAISTRAT-9001-E002\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\t## DAG Justification\n33\t\n34\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n35\t|------|------|-----------|\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 → RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 | Data/artifact dependency | The auto-refresh mechanism operates on the status surface (per-model status column and status detail view) delivered by the P0 status-surface epic. |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 → RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 | Data/artifact dependency | Filter/sort by status operates on the per-model status column the P0 status-surface epic adds to the deployed models list. |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 → RHAISTRAT-9001-E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | The documentation must describe the status values, detail view, and troubleshooting flow as actually built. |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 → RHAISTRAT-9001-E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | The documentation must reflect the refresh behavior users actually experience. |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 → RHAISTRAT-9001-E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | The documentation must reflect the list controls users actually see. Per the docs-authoring priority exception, none of these edges propagate priority; E002 derives P1 from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major`. |\n41\t\n42\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n43\t\n44\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic |\n45\t|-----|----------|------------------------|------|\n46\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) shown per deployed model in model serving views | RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 |\n47\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Status detail view with condition messages and recent events | RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 |\n48\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Status reflects InferenceService state within 30s without manual reload | RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 |\n49\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Filter and sort deployed models list by status | RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 |\n50\t| HLR-5 | P2 | Product documentation for status values and Failed troubleshooting | RHAISTRAT-9001-E002 |\n51\t\n52\tAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n53\t\n54\t## Decomposition Notes\n55\t\n56\t- **Triage (Step 0):** Not below-threshold. Although the implementation scope is a single active component owned by a single team with strong AI-implementability signals, HLR-5 requires substantive documentation authoring (a new product documentation topic explaining status values and troubleshooting steps) — a distinct work stream from code implementation that warrants its own PR review cycle. Check 2 (docs-only) does not fire because the Dashboard requires code changes.\n57\t- **KServe is a passive component.** The Affected Components list includes KServe, but the strategy states KServe already exposes the needed InferenceService status conditions and events; no KServe code changes are needed (confirmed by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`, which documents `Ready`/`PredictorReady` status conditions and Kubernetes events as existing interfaces). Validation that the Dashboard's status mapping matches the actual InferenceService status conditions and events is therefore an acceptance criterion on the nearest active component's epic (RHAISTRAT-9001-E001). The strategy assigns no validation role to the KServe owning team, so no separate validation epic is generated.\n58\t- **Priority split applied across the Dashboard epics.** HLR-3 (P1, 30-second auto-refresh) and HLR-4 (P2, filter/sort) are distinct deferrable features, not incidental polish on the P0 status surface: bundling them at P0 would prevent the P0 status surface from shipping without the P2 filter/sort work. The implementation scope is therefore split by priority tier into RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 (P0, HLR-1/HLR-2 status column and detail view), RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 (P1, HLR-3 auto-refresh), and RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 (P2, HLR-4 filter/sort), each independently plannable and deferrable while sharing the Dashboard component and team. (Revision: the initial decomposition bundled all four HLRs into one epic; the adversarial review flagged the priority collapse and this split is the correction.)\n59\t- **Component mapping:** epic components are copied verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`: `Dashboard` for E001, `Documentation` for E002. The strategy's \"KServe\" affected component maps to no epic because it is passive (see above).\n60\t- **No Investigation epics.** The strategy's Open Questions section states \"None blocking\"; no conditional ADRs, pending reviews, or risks tables are present. No unknown changes which downstream epics exist or what they do.\n61\t- **Team assumption for E002:** the strategy contains no Impacted Teams table. The documentation epic is assigned to RHOAI Dashboard, the team that owns the feature being documented and performs the mandatory technical review; adjust if a dedicated documentation team owns this content.\n62\t\n63\t## Health Warnings\n64\t\n65\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy omits the Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then with \"measured by\" clauses), and Non-Functional Requirements sections. The decomposition proceeded from the HLR table, Affected Components list, Out of Scope list, and Open Questions; per-epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n66\t- **Out-of-scope boundary relied on for ACs:** alerting/notifications, status history/timeline views, and ModelMesh deployments are explicitly out of scope; acceptance criteria on E001 enforce that the status surface covers KServe InferenceService deployments only.\n67\t- No priority inversions detected. No scope traps detected (no infrastructure implied beyond existing Dashboard and KServe components, both present in architecture context).\n68\t\n69\t## Tiered Delivery\n70\t\n71\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing. Both affected components are in the platform (architecture context files exist for Dashboard and KServe), and no upstream contributions are required.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad81c1b4d673afa0","agent_id":"a490a6d58cdfab89f","session_id":"43f64084-1d69-4055-a8f7-bc56aec5e245","uuid":"bdda1d79-8432-4a2d-8367-3a05afe4f683","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:00.805Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1dcb99e6ab1d32","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
