{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa827ed1109c690b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E001\n3\ttitle: Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe InferenceService models directly in the RHOAI Dashboard model serving views, so data scientists can tell whether a deployment is healthy without leaving the console or using `oc` / Kubernetes events. It adds a per-model status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) to the deployed models views and a status detail view exposing the underlying condition messages and recent events for failed or progressing deployments.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Derive a deployment status of Ready, Progressing, or Failed for each deployed KServe InferenceService from the InferenceService CR status conditions (e.g., Ready, PredictorReady) and recent Kubernetes events, as exposed by KServe today — no KServe-side changes.\n38\t- Display the derived status for each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n39\t- Add a status detail view that shows the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n40\t- Validate that the Dashboard's status mapping matches the actual InferenceService status conditions and Kubernetes events (KServe is passive in this strategy — this validation is part of this epic's deliverable, not a KServe change).\n41\t- Out of scope: alerting or notifications on status transitions; status history / timeline views; ModelMesh deployments (KServe InferenceService only).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a deployed model whose InferenceService is Ready, when the user opens the model serving view, then the model is shown with status Ready.\n46\t- Given a model whose deployment is failed or progressing, when the user opens the status detail view, then the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent Kubernetes events are shown.\n47\t- The status mapping (Ready / Progressing / Failed derivation) is validated against actual InferenceService CR status conditions and Kubernetes events as documented for KServe, with no changes required to KServe.\n48\t- No status-related alerts/notifications, status history, or timeline views are introduced by this change.\n49\t- ModelMesh deployments are not covered by the status surface (KServe InferenceService only).\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-1 (P0): Users see a deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n54\t- HLR-2 (P0): Users can open a status detail view showing the underlying condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad81c1b4d673afa0","agent_id":"a490a6d58cdfab89f","session_id":"43f64084-1d69-4055-a8f7-bc56aec5e245","uuid":"a2d0b164-b64f-433a-803e-941ca05eefd6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:05.122Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa827ed1109c690b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
