 conditions and events it exposes.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Every status value displayed for deployed models in the Dashboard model serving views (Ready, Progressing, Failed) is explained in the documentation.\n49\t- The documentation includes first troubleshooting steps for Failed deployments.\n50\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented Dashboard behavior and validated for accuracy against the KServe InferenceService status conditions and events the status surface is built on.\n51\t- The documentation is published through the Red Hat docs content process.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-5 (P2): Product documentation explains each status value and the first troubleshooting steps for Failed deployments.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad81c1b4d673afa0","agent_id":"a490a6d58cdfab89f","session_id":"43f64084-1d69-4055-a8f7-bc56aec5e245","uuid":"a811f66d-6770-4c95-8a24-b5f3056eb10a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:06.179Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f56a8bfe9bd4e8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
