{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86eafea92d7b4ea6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E003\n3\ttitle: Near-real-time refresh of deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: null\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9001-E001\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Near-real-time refresh of deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers automatic refresh of the deployment status displayed in the RHOAI Dashboard model serving views, so the status a data scientist sees reflects the actual KServe InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload. It builds on the deployed-model status surface (per-model status column and status detail view) delivered by the P0 status-surface work for model serving.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Implement automatic refresh of the derived deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) shown in the Dashboard model serving views, so the displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change.\n39\t- The status detail view (underlying condition messages and recent events) for a failed or progressing deployment also reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change.\n40\t- No manual page reload is required for the displayed status or detail view to update.\n41\t- No KServe-side changes: the InferenceService status conditions and Kubernetes events are consumed as exposed by KServe today.\n42\t- Out of scope: alerting or notifications on status transitions; status history / timeline views; ModelMesh deployments (KServe InferenceService only).\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given a change in the actual InferenceService state of a deployed model, when 30 seconds have elapsed, then the status displayed in the model serving views reflects the new state without a manual page reload.\n47\t- Given a failed or progressing deployment whose underlying conditions or events change, when the status detail view is open, then the condition messages and recent events shown reflect the new state within 30 seconds without a manual page reload.\n48\t- The refresh mechanism is implemented Dashboard-side only, with no changes required to KServe.\n49\t- No status-related alerts/notifications, status history, or timeline views are introduced by this change.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-3 (P1): Displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad81c1b4d673afa0","agent_id":"a490a6d58cdfab89f","session_id":"43f64084-1d69-4055-a8f7-bc56aec5e245","uuid":"93c4da7d-0fd5-4a0f-998a-fd6012d5481e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:09.957Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86eafea92d7b4ea6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
