mixed statuses, when the user filters by status Failed, then only models with status Failed are shown.\n46\t- Given the deployed models list, when the user sorts by status, then the list is ordered by status accordingly.\n47\t- Given no filter or sort selected, when the user opens the deployed models list, then the default unfiltered and unsorted list is shown.\n48\t- No status-related alerts/notifications, status history, or timeline views are introduced by this change.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-4 (P2): Users can filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad81c1b4d673afa0","agent_id":"a490a6d58cdfab89f","session_id":"43f64084-1d69-4055-a8f7-bc56aec5e245","uuid":"0b5630f8-22f0-4f93-8a1d-35f3d1928483","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:11.077Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab226beb1144b6fb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
